<LevelHeader>
  type = Level
  name = The Black Ops Chronomancer
  description = 
  notReplayable = True
  timestamp = 133753129738660520
</LevelHeader>
<Tips>
  Tricking Liv will get easier as more allies show up, so it's fine to focus on survival, dealing with reinforcements, and gaining mana early on.
  Since you can see who Liv plans to swap with when you attack her, you're looking for attacks that will harm her when she swaps to that position.
  Liv won't swap with the wizard you have selected, so you can change her swap target by selecting someone else. She wants you to shoot each other.
  Liv knows Zan's Predictive Shot well, and will duck if she has time to see it coming for her. Anything that puts her in the beam instantly will work, though.
  If Liv will swap with Zan, line him up so he can aim Predictive Shot directly away from her. Attack with someone else, and she'll swap into the beam.
  Try a Chain Shock through Liv and her swap target, where the swap target is going to take the worse hit. Liv will take that hit instead when she swaps.
  Banks' Transference applies instantly, so Liv can't dodge it. Make her the victim, then hit the protectee hard - maybe a Dall charge?
  When Liv cheats death, the new Liv will seek cover to get her bearings. This turn, she'll be harder to kill again, but won't attack.
  If you cast Swap on Liv, she Swaps with her Swap target first and you Swap with them instead. If you can find a use for that, you're smarter than us.
</Tips>

